<!--
  CJHQ sitemap

  lastmod: keep these honest. Google uses lastmod when it is accurate and
  starts ignoring it site-wide when it is not, so do not bulk-update every
  date on each deploy. Change a page's date only when that page's content
  actually changes.

  2026-08-28: all eight updated together because every route file was
  regenerated on that date (each now marks its own page active in the raw
  HTML, not the homepage). That is a genuine change to every page, so a
  shared date is accurate here rather than a bulk refresh for its own sake.

  changefreq / priority: Google ignores both. Retained because Bing still
  reads them and they cost nothing.

  hreflang: /fr/ is the one distinct French URL, added 2026-08-28. It is the
  French homepage, and it is reciprocal with / via hreflang tags in both files.
  The other seven routes have no French equivalent and deliberately carry no
  hreflang - pointing fr at an English URL would be wrong, and inventing
  /fr/about would mean shipping pages that do not exist. See the note in-->
